@* ============================================================================
   Applies to EVERY view in this folder and below.

   Django: there is no equivalent. Each template repeats its own {% load %}
   tags, and there is no way to make a `{% load %}` hierarchical.

   @using          -> makes namespaces available, so views can write
                      `Title.Mr` instead of `Remus.Mvc.Data.Title.Mr`
   @addTagHelper   -> switches on the asp-* attributes. Without this line,
                      <form asp-action="Login"> renders literally as an
                      unknown attribute and silently posts to the current URL.
                      Django's {% load %} fails loudly; this one fails quietly.
   ============================================================================ *@

@using Remus.Mvc
@using Remus.Mvc.Models
@using Remus.Mvc.Data
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Rendering
@addTagHelper *, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers
